==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|modifien}}, from {{etyl|fr}} {{term|modifier}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|modificare||to limit, control, regulate, deponent}}, from {{term|modificari||to measure off, set bound to, moderate}}, from {{term|modus||measure}} + {{term|facere||to make}}; see [[mode]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-modify.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|modif|i|ed}}

# {{transitive}} To [[make]] partial [[change]]s to.
# {{intransitive}} To [[be]] or [[become]] modified.

====Synonyms====
* [[adapt]], [[alter]], [[amend]], [[revamp]], [[rework]]

====Related terms====
* [[modification]]
* [[modifier]]

